import{_ as e,o as a,c as r,a0 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BTg7EidG.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"The Bestiary","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guide/bestiary.md","filePath":"guide/bestiary.md"}'),n={name:"guide/bestiary.md"};function o(i,t,d,h,l,g){return a(),r("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[s('<h1 id="the-bestiary" tabindex="-1">The Bestiary <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-bestiary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Bestiary&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The alchemists of old did not stop at metals. Their creations — and their escapes — still walk the world.</p><h2 id="creature-lairs" tabindex="-1">Creature lairs <a class="header-anchor" href="#creature-lairs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Creature lairs&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Five great lairs stand in the wilds, each heavily warded and each home to one of the great creatures:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Lair</th><th>Creature</th><th>Fights like</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Golem Foundry</td><td><strong>Brass Golem</strong></td><td>An anvil with fists — huge, armored, slow</td></tr><tr><td>Salamander Vent</td><td><strong>Salamander</strong></td><td>A walking furnace — searing ranged fire</td></tr><tr><td>Basilisk Pit</td><td><strong>Basilisk</strong></td><td>The crowned serpent — venom at speed</td></tr><tr><td>Quicksilver Well</td><td><strong>Quicksilver Elemental</strong></td><td>Living mercury — faster than any rider</td></tr><tr><td>Chimera Vats</td><td><strong>Chimera</strong></td><td>Three beasts stitched into one fury</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Capture a lair, march a party onto it and open <strong>Recruit</strong>: the beast that lives there is on the bench like any other hire — for a fortune up front and a <strong>ruinous daily gold upkeep</strong>. Miss a day&#39;s pay and the creature <strong>rampages</strong>: it mauls its own party for half their health, then abandons you. Feed your monsters.</p><p>A beast is bought, never sworn: it costs no Follower, and it can never be mustered from a holding or sent as a reinforcement. You go to the lair, or you go without.</p><h2 id="the-wilds" tabindex="-1">The Wilds <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-wilds" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Wilds&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Packs of <strong>Homunculi</strong> — vat-spill given legs, the little horrors of the wastes — roam the world and hunt any party they find, sometimes with an escaped creature among them. They belong to no guild, take no gifts, and cannot be tamed.</p><h2 id="the-beastmaster" tabindex="-1">The Beastmaster <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-beastmaster" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Beastmaster&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Any city grown to <strong>level 3</strong> attracts a <strong>Beastmaster</strong> — hire one into a party from that city&#39;s <strong>Recruit</strong> bench (200🪙 and a Follower).</p><p>They are no soldier. A Beastmaster barely swings, and carries only a <strong>knife, a herding stave and charms</strong>: their trade is the snare. What they are worth is what they bring back alive — and the stave is there because a keeper&#39;s work is arts, which is what a staff is for.</p><ul><li><strong>After a won battle</strong>, each downed <em>creature</em> has a chance of being taken alive and joining you, upkeep and all. Homunculi are never worth keeping; the Beastmaster won&#39;t even try.</li><li><strong>Setting a snare</strong> — the command bar&#39;s 🪤 <strong>Set Trap</strong>, on open ground away from any holding — baits something out of the wild. It costs the whole day&#39;s marching, and there is no declining it: the fight opens at once, and the quarry moves first.</li></ul><p>On the field the Beastmaster gains a <strong>🪤 Snare</strong> action against a beast standing next to them. <strong>The weaker the beast, the likelier it goes into the sack</strong> — wear it down first, but do not kill it: a dead beast ends the battle with nothing to show. A successful snare ends the fight then and there and the beast is yours.</p><p><strong>Trapper&#39;s tools</strong> — snare-cords, torcs, muzzles — are accessories that add to those odds, and they only ever turn up as loot for a party that keeps a Beastmaster.</p><h2 id="taming" tabindex="-1">Taming <a class="header-anchor" href="#taming" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Taming&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A beast learns no trade. What it earns instead is <strong>tameness</strong> — it gets used to its keepers — and a settled beast is far cheaper to feed. Keep one in a Beastmaster&#39;s company and it settles a little further every day.</p><p>Each kind also brings a trick nobody teaches it:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Beast</th><th>Its own art</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Chimera</td><td><strong>Venom</strong> — the bite keeps working for three more turns</td></tr><tr><td>Basilisk</td><td><strong>Petrifying Gaze</strong> — one look and they cannot take a step</td></tr><tr><td>Salamander</td><td><strong>Ember Breath</strong> — fire over a three-tile square</td></tr><tr><td>Quicksilver Elemental</td><td><strong>Quicksilver Surge</strong> — strikes, then moves again</td></tr><tr><td>Brass Golem</td><td><strong>Brazen Guard</strong> — +3 guard to itself and everyone beside it</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Homunculi can be snared too. They are vat-spill and they learn nothing, but they have legs and they can be made to carry a spear.</p><h2 id="the-bestiary-1" tabindex="-1">The Bestiary <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-bestiary-1" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Bestiary&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Raise a <strong>Bestiary</strong> in a city&#39;s ring (220🪙 and 20💎 at a level-2 city): a keepers&#39; hall with stalls, a paddock and a feed trough. Post Followers to it as you would to any craft.</p><p>A level-3 city with <strong>four keepers</strong> posted to its Bestiary opens <strong>beast lore</strong> for research — skills no hall will teach you:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Beast Bond</strong></td><td>Every beast in the hero&#39;s party fights at +3 attack and +3 defence</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Wild Heart</strong></td><td>Beasts feed for half the gold and mend 15% of their health a day</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Quickening Balm</strong></td><td>Shared with the alchemists — see below</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These belong to a Beastmaster <strong>raised to Champion</strong>, and to no one else. A Beastmaster can be promoted like any other veteran.</p><h2 id="the-quickening-balm" tabindex="-1">The Quickening Balm <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-quickening-balm" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Quickening Balm&quot;">​</a></h2><p>An alchemist&#39;s study (researched at a level-2 hall) that a Beastmaster shares. On the battlefield it is laid on <strong>ground</strong>, not on a body, and soaks in <strong>three battlefield turns later</strong> — turns of the fight, not of your own — healing everyone standing in that patch when it settles.</p><p>The delay is the point: you are committing to where your wounded <em>will</em> be, not where they are. In a Beastmaster&#39;s hands the balm tends <strong>only the beasts</strong>.</p>',28)])])}const m=e(n,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
